{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal sensor plant plus a motion plant, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. Clear sensing drives random-walk exploration by default, obstacle sensing forces one-shot turn recovery, and a small alternation spec biases steady coverage by inserting short forward pulses after random-walk while never allowing forward in obstacle-recovery states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into compact plants so synthesis can disable unsafe controllables without inventing new events",
    "Use dedicated obstacle-triggered recovery specs with one-shot turn commands and a small alternation spec to mix random_walk and move_forward for coverage"
  ],
